# text = He readily availed himself of the money which , to give her but one hour's peace of mind , I would have poured out as freely as water -- nay , he often sent her back for more -- and yet even while he squandered it , he made the very success of these , her applications to me , the groundwork of cruel taunts and jeers , protesting that he knew she thought with bitter remorse of the choice she had made , that she had married him from motives of interest and vanity ( he was a gay young man with great friends about him when she chose him for her husband ), and venting in short upon her , by every unjust and unkind means , the bitterness of that ruin and disappointment which had been brought about by his profligacy alone .
