# text = Jane Dibabs -- the Dibabses lived in the beautiful little thatched white house one story high , covered all over with ivy and creeping plants , with an exquisite little porch with twining honysuckles and all sorts of things : where the earwigs used to fall into one's tea on a summer evening , and always fell upon their backs and kicked dreadfully , and where the frogs used to get into the rushlight shades when one stopped all night , and sit up and look through the little holes like Christians -- Jane Dibabs , SHE married a man who was a great deal older than herself , and WOULD marry him , notwithstanding all that could be said to the contrary , and she was so fond of him that nothing was ever equal to it .
